{"traj_id": "deepmath-55767_0", "problem": "Evaluate the integral: $$ 4n(n-1)\\int_0^1 \\frac{1}{8t^3}\\left[\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n+1}}{(n+1)}-\\frac{t^{2n+2}}{n+1}-t^4\\{\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n-1}}{n-1}-\\frac{t^{2n-2}}{n-1} \\} \\right] dt.$$ For $n \\geq 3$, verify that the value of the integral is 1.", "gold": "1", "pred": "1", "is_correct": true, "tier": "hard", "n_tokens": 10773, "meta_leak": [], "paragraphs": ["Let me carefully evaluate this integral. Let me denote the integral as $I$ and work through it step by step.", "The integral is:\n$$I = 4n(n-1)\\int_0^1 \\frac{1}{8t^3}\\left[\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n+1}}{n+1}-\\frac{t^{2n+2}}{n+1}-t^4\\left\\{\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n-1}}{n-1}-\\frac{t^{2n-2}}{n-1} \\right\\}\\right] dt$$", "Let me simplify. First, factor out $\\frac{1}{8t^3}$:", "$$I = \\frac{4n(n-1)}{8}\\int_0^1 \\frac{1}{t^3}\\left[\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n+1} - t^{2n+2}}{n+1}-t^4\\cdot\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n-1} - t^{2n-2}}{n-1}\\right] dt$$", "$$I = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\int_0^1 \\left[\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n+1} - t^{2n+2}}{(n+1)t^3}-t\\cdot\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n-1} - t^{2n-2}}{n-1}\\right] dt$$", "Let me note that $2t - t^2 = t(2-t)$. So $(2t-t^2)^k = t^k(2-t)^k$.", "So the integral becomes:\n$$I = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\int_0^1 \\left[\\frac{t^{n+1}(2-t)^{n+1} - t^{2n+2}}{(n+1)t^3}-t\\cdot\\frac{t^{n-1}(2-t)^{n-1} - t^{2n-2}}{n-1}\\right] dt$$", "$$I = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\int_0^1 \\left[\\frac{t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1} - t^{2n-1}}{n+1}-\\frac{t^n(2-t)^{n-1} - t^{2n-1}}{n-1}\\right] dt$$", "Let me split this:\n$$I = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\left[\\frac{1}{n+1}\\int_0^1 t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1}dt - \\frac{1}{n+1}\\int_0^1 t^{2n-1}dt - \\frac{1}{n-1}\\int_0^1 t^n(2-t)^{n-1}dt + \\frac{1}{n-1}\\int_0^1 t^{2n-1}dt\\right]$$", "Let me compute the simple integrals:\n$$\\int_0^1 t^{2n-1}dt = \\frac{1}{2n}$$", "So the terms with $t^{2n-1}$:\n$$-\\frac{1}{n+1}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2n} + \\frac{1}{n-1}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2n} = \\frac{1}{2n}\\left(-\\frac{1}{n+1}+\\frac{1}{n-1}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2n}\\cdot\\frac{(n+1)-(n-1)}{(n+1)(n-1)} = \\frac{1}{2n}\\cdot\\frac{2}{n^2-1} = \\frac{1}{n(n^2-1)} = \\frac{1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}$$", "Now I need to compute:\n$$A = \\int_0^1 t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1}dt$$\n$$B = \\int_0^1 t^n(2-t)^{n-1}dt$$", "Let me use the substitution $t = 2u$ for these... actually that won't work directly since the upper limit is 1, not 2.", "Let me use the Beta function. We can write:\n$$\\int_0^1 t^a(2-t)^b dt = 2^{b}\\int_0^{1/2} u^a(1-u)^b du$$", "Wait, let me substitute $t = 2u$:\n$$\\int_0^1 t^a(2-t)^b dt = \\int_0^{1/2} (2u)^a(2-2u)^b \\cdot 2du = 2^{a+b+1}\\int_0^{1/2} u^a(1-u)^b du$$", "So:\n$$A = 2^{n+1+n+1}\\int_0^{1/2} u^{n-2}(1-u)^{n+1}du = 2^{2n+2}\\int_0^{1/2} u^{n-2}(1-u)^{n+1}du$$", "$$B = 2^{n+n-1+1}\\int_0^{1/2} u^n(1-u)^{n-1}du = 2^{2n}\\int_0^{1/2} u^n(1-u)^{n-1}du$$", "Hmm, these are incomplete Beta functions which are hard to evaluate directly. Let me think of another approach.", "Actually, let me use the binomial expansion approach.\n\nFor $A = \\int_0^1 t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1}dt$:\n$(2-t)^{n+1} = \\sum_{k=0}^{n+1}\\binom{n+1}{k}2^{n+1-k}(-t)^k = \\sum_{k=0}^{n+1}\\binom{n+1}{k}2^{n+1-k}(-1)^k t^k$", "So $A = \\sum_{k=0}^{n+1}\\binom{n+1}{k}2^{n+1-k}(-1)^k\\int_0^1 t^{n-2+k}dt = \\sum_{k=0}^{n+1}\\binom{n+1}{k}2^{n+1-k}(-1)^k\\frac{1}{n-1+k}$", "For $B = \\int_0^1 t^n(2-t)^{n-1}dt$:\n$(2-t)^{n-1} = \\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}\\binom{n-1}{j}2^{n-1-j}(-t)^j$", "So $B = \\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}\\binom{n-1}{j}2^{n-1-j}(-1)^j\\int_0^1 t^{n+j}dt = \\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}\\binom{n-1}{j}2^{n-1-j}(-1)^j\\frac{1}{n+1+j}$", "This is getting messy. Let me try a different approach.\n\nLet me try integration by parts or find a relationship between $A$ and $B$.", "Actually, let me try a different substitution. Let $t = 2s$ in a different way, or let me try to relate $A$ and $B$.", "Notice that:\n$A = \\int_0^1 t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1}dt = \\int_0^1 t^{n-2}(2-t)\\cdot(2-t)^n dt = 2\\int_0^1 t^{n-2}(2-t)^n dt - \\int_0^1 t^{n-1}(2-t)^n dt$", "And $B = \\int_0^1 t^n(2-t)^{n-1}dt = \\int_0^1 t^n(2-t)\\cdot(2-t)^{n-2}dt = 2\\int_0^1 t^n(2-t)^{n-2}dt - \\int_0^1 t^{n+1}(2-t)^{n-2}dt$", "This is still complicated. Let me try yet another approach.\n\nLet me define $C(a,b) = \\int_0^1 t^a(2-t)^b dt$ for various $a, b$.", "Actually, let me try a substitution $u = 1-t$ or something.", "For $A = \\int_0^1 t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1}dt$, let $u = 1-t$, so $t = 1-u$, $dt = -du$:\n$A = \\int_0^1 (1-u)^{n-2}(1+u)^{n+1}du$", "For $B = \\int_0^1 t^n(2-t)^{n-1}dt$, let $u = 1-t$:\n$B = \\int_0^1 (1-u)^n(1+u)^{n-1}du$", "Hmm, let me expand these:\n$(1-u)^{n-2}(1+u)^{n+1} = (1-u)^{n-2}(1+u)^{n-2}(1+u)^3 = (1-u^2)^{n-2}(1+u)^3$", "$(1-u)^n(1+u)^{n-1} = (1-u)(1-u^2)^{n-1}$", "So:\n$A = \\int_0^1 (1-u^2)^{n-2}(1+u)^3 du$\n$B = \\int_0^1 (1-u)(1-u^2)^{n-1} du$", "Now let $v = u^2$, $dv = 2u\\,du$, $du = dv/(2\\sqrt{v})$:", "For $A$:\n$A = \\int_0^1 (1-v)^{n-2}(1+\\sqrt{v})^3 \\frac{dv}{2\\sqrt{v}}$", "This is still not great. Let me try expanding differently.\n\nActually, let me try to directly compute $A$ and $B$ using the relation:\n$(1-u^2)^{n-2}(1+u)^3 = (1-u)^{n-2}(1+u)^{n+1}$", "Let me expand $(1-u)^{n-2}(1+u)^{n+1}$:\n$= (1-u)^{n-2}(1+u)^{n-2}(1+u)^3$\n$= (1-u^2)^{n-2}(1+u)^3$\n$= (1-u^2)^{n-2}(1+3u+3u^2+u^3)$", "And $(1-u)(1-u^2)^{n-1} = (1-u^{2n-1})... $", "No wait: $(1-u)(1-u^2)^{n-1} = (1-u)\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\\binom{n-1}{k}(-u^2)^k$", "Let me try a different approach. Let me use the fact that:\n$\\int_0^1 (1-u^2)^{m} du = \\frac{\\sqrt{\\pi}\\,\\Gamma(m+1)}{2\\Gamma(m+3/2)}$", "And $\\int_0^1 u(1-u^2)^m du = \\frac{1}{2}\\int_0^1 v^0(1-v)^m dv = \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{1}{m+1} = \\frac{1}{2(m+1)}$", "And $\\int_0^1 u^2(1-u^2)^m du = \\frac{1}{2}\\int_0^1 v^{1/2}(1-v)^m dv = \\frac{1}{2}B(3/2, m+1) = \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{\\Gamma(3/2)\\Gamma(m+1)}{\\Gamma(m+5/2)}$", "And $\\int_0^1 u^3(1-u^2)^m du = \\frac{1}{2}\\int_0^1 v(1-v)^m dv = \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{1}{(m+1)(m+2)} = \\frac{1}{2(m+1)(m+2)}$", "Now:\n$A = \\int_0^1 (1-u^2)^{n-2}(1+3u+3u^2+u^3)du$\n$= \\int_0^1 (1-u^2)^{n-2}du + 3\\int_0^1 u(1-u^2)^{n-2}du + 3\\int_0^1 u^2(1-u^2)^{n-2}du + \\int_0^1 u^3(1-u^2)^{n-2}du$", "With $m = n-2$:\n$A = I_0(n-2) + 3\\cdot\\frac{1}{2(n-1)} + 3\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{\\Gamma(3/2)\\Gamma(n-1)}{\\Gamma(n+1/2)} + \\frac{1}{2(n-1)(n)}$", "where $I_0(m) = \\int_0^1 (1-u^2)^m du = \\frac{\\sqrt{\\pi}\\,\\Gamma(m+1)}{2\\Gamma(m+3/2)}$", "And $B = \\int_0^1 (1-u)(1-u^2)^{n-1}du = \\int_0^1 (1-u^2)^{n-1}du - \\int_0^1 u(1-u^2)^{n-1}du$\n$= I_0(n-1) - \\frac{1}{2n}$", "where $I_0(n-1) = \\frac{\\sqrt{\\pi}\\,\\Gamma(n)}{2\\Gamma(n+1/2)}$", "This is getting very complicated with Gamma functions. Let me try a completely different approach.", "Let me go back to the original integral and try to simplify it differently.", "Actually, let me re-examine the original integral more carefully.\n\n$$I = 4n(n-1)\\int_0^1 \\frac{1}{8t^3}\\left[\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n+1}}{n+1}-\\frac{t^{2n+2}}{n+1}-t^4\\left\\{\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n-1}}{n-1}-\\frac{t^{2n-2}}{n-1} \\right\\}\\right] dt$$", "Let me factor out constants:\n$= \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\int_0^1 \\frac{1}{t^3}\\left[\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n+1} - t^{2n+2}}{n+1} - \\frac{t^4[(2t-t^2)^{n-1} - t^{2n-2}]}{n-1}\\right]dt$", "$= \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\int_0^1 \\left[\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n+1} - t^{2n+2}}{(n+1)t^3} - \\frac{t(2t-t^2)^{n-1} - t^{2n-1}}{n-1}\\right]dt$", "Now using $(2t-t^2)^k = t^k(2-t)^k$:", "$= \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\int_0^1 \\left[\\frac{t^{n+1}(2-t)^{n+1} - t^{2n+2}}{(n+1)t^3} - \\frac{t\\cdot t^{n-1}(2-t)^{n-1} - t^{2n-1}}{n-1}\\right]dt$", "$= \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\int_0^1 \\left[\\frac{t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1} - t^{2n-1}}{n+1} - \\frac{t^n(2-t)^{n-1} - t^{2n-1}}{n-1}\\right]dt$", "$= \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\left[\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{1}{(n+1)2n} - \\frac{B}{n-1} + \\frac{1}{(n-1)2n}\\right]$", "where $A = \\int_0^1 t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1}dt$ and $B = \\int_0^1 t^n(2-t)^{n-1}dt$.", "The $t^{2n-1}$ terms:\n$-\\frac{1}{(n+1)2n} + \\frac{1}{(n-1)2n} = \\frac{1}{2n}\\left(\\frac{1}{n-1}-\\frac{1}{n+1}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2n}\\cdot\\frac{2}{n^2-1} = \\frac{1}{n(n^2-1)}$", "So:\n$I = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\left[\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} + \\frac{1}{n(n^2-1)}\\right]$", "$= \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\cdot\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\cdot\\frac{B}{n-1} + \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\cdot\\frac{1}{n(n^2-1)}$", "$= \\frac{n(n-1)A}{2(n+1)} - \\frac{nB}{2} + \\frac{n-1}{2(n+1)}$", "$= \\frac{n(n-1)A - n(n+1)B + (n-1)}{2(n+1)}$", "So I need to show that $n(n-1)A - n(n+1)B + (n-1) = 2(n+1)$, i.e.:\n$n(n-1)A - n(n+1)B = 2(n+1) - (n-1) = 2n+2-n+1 = n+3$", "Hmm, that doesn't look clean. Let me recheck.\n\nWait, I want $I = 1$, so:\n$\\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\left[\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} + \\frac{1}{n(n^2-1)}\\right] = 1$", "$\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} + \\frac{1}{n(n^2-1)} = \\frac{2}{n(n-1)}$", "$\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} = \\frac{2}{n(n-1)} - \\frac{1}{n(n^2-1)} = \\frac{2}{n(n-1)} - \\frac{1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}$", "$= \\frac{2(n+1)-1}{n(n-1)(n+1)} = \\frac{2n+1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}$", "So I need: $\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} = \\frac{2n+1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}$", "Or equivalently: $n(n-1)A - n(n+1)B = 2n+1$", "Let me verify this by computing $A$ and $B$ for small values of $n$.", "For $n = 3$:\n$A = \\int_0^1 t^1(2-t)^4 dt$\n$(2-t)^4 = 16 - 32t + 24t^2 - 8t^3 + t^4$\n$A = \\int_0^1 t(16-32t+24t^2-8t^3+t^4)dt = \\int_0^1 (16t-32t^2+24t^3-8t^4+t^5)dt$\n$= 8 - \\frac{32}{3} + 6 - 2 + \\frac{1}{6} = 8 + 6 - 2 + \\frac{1}{6} - \\frac{32}{3}$\n$= 12 + \\frac{1}{6} - \\frac{64}{6} = 12 - \\frac{63}{6} = 12 - \\frac{21}{2} = \\frac{24-21}{2} = \\frac{3}{2}$", "$B = \\int_0^1 t^3(2-t)^2 dt$\n$(2-t)^2 = 4-4t+t^2$\n$B = \\int_0^1 (4t^3-4t^4+t^5)dt = 1 - 1 + \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{6}$", "Check: $n(n-1)A - n(n+1)B = 3\\cdot 2\\cdot\\frac{3}{2} - 3\\cdot 4\\cdot\\frac{1}{6} = 9 - 2 = 7$", "And $2n+1 = 7$. ✓\n\nLet me verify for $n = 4$:\n$A = \\int_0^1 t^2(2-t)^5 dt$\n$(2-t)^5 = 32-80t+80t^2-40t^3+10t^4-t^5$\n$t^2(2-t)^5 = 32t^2-80t^3+80t^4-40t^5+10t^6-t^7$\n$A = \\frac{32}{3}-\\frac{80}{4}+\\frac{80}{5}-\\frac{40}{6}+\\frac{10}{7}-\\frac{1}{8}$\n$= \\frac{32}{3}-20+16-\\frac{20}{3}+\\frac{10}{7}-\\frac{1}{8}$\n$= \\frac{12}{3}-4+\\frac{10}{7}-\\frac{1}{8}$\n$= 4-4+\\frac{10}{7}-\\frac{1}{8}$\n$= \\frac{10}{7}-\\frac{1}{8} = \\frac{80-7}{56} = \\frac{73}{56}$", "$B = \\int_0^1 t^4(2-t)^3 dt$\n$(2-t)^3 = 8-12t+6t^2-t^3$\n$t^4(2-t)^3 = 8t^4-12t^5+6t^6-t^7$\n$B = \\frac{8}{5}-\\frac{12}{6}+\\frac{6}{7}-\\frac{1}{8} = \\frac{8}{5}-2+\\frac{6}{7}-\\frac{1}{8}$\n$= \\frac{8}{5}-2+\\frac{6}{7}-\\frac{1}{8}$\n$= \\frac{1120-560+210-35}{560} = \\frac{735}{560} = \\frac{21}{16}$", "Wait let me recompute: $\\frac{8}{5} - 2 + \\frac{6}{7} - \\frac{1}{8}$\n$= \\frac{8}{5} - 2 + \\frac{6}{7} - \\frac{1}{8}$\nCommon denominator: 280\n$= \\frac{448}{280} - \\frac{560}{280} + \\frac{240}{280} - \\frac{35}{280}$\n$= \\frac{448-560+240-35}{280} = \\frac{93}{280}$", "Check: $n(n-1)A - n(n+1)B = 4\\cdot 3\\cdot\\frac{73}{56} - 4\\cdot 5\\cdot\\frac{93}{280}$\n$= \\frac{876}{56} - \\frac{1860}{280}$\n$= \\frac{4380}{280} - \\frac{1860}{280} = \\frac{2520}{280} = 9$", "And $2n+1 = 9$. ✓\n\nSo the identity $n(n-1)A - n(n+1)B = 2n+1$ holds. Now let me prove it.", "We need to show:\n$n(n-1)\\int_0^1 t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1}dt - n(n+1)\\int_0^1 t^n(2-t)^{n-1}dt = 2n+1$", "Let me use integration by parts on these integrals.\n\nFor $A = \\int_0^1 t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1}dt$:", "Let $u = (2-t)^{n+1}$, $dv = t^{n-2}dt$\n$du = -(n+1)(2-t)^n dt$, $v = \\frac{t^{n-1}}{n-1}$", "$A = \\left[\\frac{t^{n-1}(2-t)^{n+1}}{n-1}\\right]_0^1 + \\frac{n+1}{n-1}\\int_0^1 t^{n-1}(2-t)^n dt$", "$= \\frac{1^{n-1}\\cdot 1^{n+1}}{n-1} - 0 + \\frac{n+1}{n-1}\\int_0^1 t^{n-1}(2-t)^n dt$", "$= \\frac{1}{n-1} + \\frac{n+1}{n-1}\\int_0^1 t^{n-1}(2-t)^n dt$", "Let me denote $C = \\int_0^1 t^{n-1}(2-t)^n dt$.", "For $B = \\int_0^1 t^n(2-t)^{n-1}dt$:", "Let $u = t^n$, $dv = (2-t)^{n-1}dt$\n$du = nt^{n-1}dt$, $v = -\\frac{(2-t)^n}{n}$", "$B = \\left[-\\frac{t^n(2-t)^n}{n}\\right]_0^1 + \\int_0^1 t^{n-1}(2-t)^n dt$", "$= -\\frac{1\\cdot 1}{n} + 0 + C = C - \\frac{1}{n}$", "So $B = C - \\frac{1}{n}$, which means $C = B + \\frac{1}{n}$.", "And $A = \\frac{1}{n-1} + \\frac{n+1}{n-1}\\left(B + \\frac{1}{n}\\right) = \\frac{1}{n-1} + \\frac{(n+1)B}{n-1} + \\frac{n+1}{n(n-1)}$", "$= \\frac{n + (n+1)B + n+1}{n(n-1)} = \\frac{2n+1 + (n+1)B}{n(n-1)}$", "So $n(n-1)A = 2n+1 + (n+1)B$", "Therefore: $n(n-1)A - n(n+1)B = 2n+1 + (n+1)B - n(n+1)B = 2n+1 + (n+1)(1-n)B$", "Wait, that gives $2n+1 - (n-1)(n+1)B = 2n+1 - (n^2-1)B$.", "But we need this to equal $2n+1$, which would require $B = 0$, which is not true.", "Let me recheck my integration by parts.\n\nFor $A = \\int_0^1 t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1}dt$:\n$u = (2-t)^{n+1}$, $du = -(n+1)(2-t)^n dt$\n$dv = t^{n-2}dt$, $v = \\frac{t^{n-1}}{n-1}$", "$\\int u\\, dv = uv - \\int v\\, du$", "$A = \\left[\\frac{t^{n-1}(2-t)^{n+1}}{n-1}\\right]_0^1 - \\int_0^1 \\frac{t^{n-1}}{n-1}\\cdot[-(n+1)(2-t)^n]dt$", "$= \\frac{1}{n-1} + \\frac{n+1}{n-1}\\int_0^1 t^{n-1}(2-t)^n dt$", "At $t=1$: $\\frac{1^{n-1}\\cdot(2-1)^{n+1}}{n-1} = \\frac{1}{n-1}$ ✓\nAt $t=0$: $\\frac{0^{n-1}\\cdot(2)^{n+1}}{n-1} = 0$ (for $n \\geq 3$, $n-1 \\geq 2 > 0$) ✓", "For $B = \\int_0^1 t^n(2-t)^{n-1}dt$:\n$u = t^n$, $du = nt^{n-1}dt$\n$dv = (2-t)^{n-1}dt$, $v = -\\frac{(2-t)^n}{n}$", "$B = \\left[-\\frac{t^n(2-t)^n}{n}\\right]_0^1 - \\int_0^1 -\\frac{(2-t)^n}{n}\\cdot nt^{n-1}dt$", "$= -\\frac{1^n\\cdot 1^n}{n} - 0 + \\int_0^1 t^{n-1}(2-t)^n dt$", "$= -\\frac{1}{n} + C$\n\nSo $B = C - \\frac{1}{n}$, hence $C = B + \\frac{1}{n}$.", "And $A = \\frac{1}{n-1} + \\frac{n+1}{n-1}\\left(B + \\frac{1}{n}\\right)$", "$= \\frac{1}{n-1} + \\frac{(n+1)B}{n-1} + \\frac{n+1}{n(n-1)}$", "$= \\frac{n}{n(n-1)} + \\frac{(n+1)B}{n-1} + \\frac{n+1}{n(n-1)}$", "$= \\frac{n+n+1}{n(n-1)} + \\frac{(n+1)B}{n-1}$", "$= \\frac{2n+1}{n(n-1)} + \\frac{(n+1)B}{n-1}$", "So $n(n-1)A = 2n+1 + n(n+1)B$", "Therefore: $n(n-1)A - n(n+1)B = 2n+1$ ✓", "So the identity holds. Let me now put it all together.\n\nGoing back:\n$I = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\left[\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} + \\frac{1}{n(n^2-1)}\\right]$", "We showed $n(n-1)A = 2n+1 + n(n+1)B$, so:\n$\\frac{n(n-1)A}{n+1} = \\frac{2n+1}{n+1} + nB$", "$\\frac{A}{n+1} = \\frac{2n+1}{n(n+1)} + B$", "So:\n$\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} = \\frac{2n+1}{n(n+1)} + B - \\frac{B}{n-1} = \\frac{2n+1}{n(n+1)} + B\\left(1 - \\frac{1}{n-1}\\right)$", "$= \\frac{2n+1}{n(n+1)} + B\\cdot\\frac{n-2}{n-1}$", "Hmm, this doesn't immediately simplify to $\\frac{2n+1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}$ unless $B = 0$ or $n = 2$.", "Wait, let me recheck. I think I made an error somewhere. Let me recompute.", "We need:\n$\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} + \\frac{1}{n(n^2-1)} = \\frac{2}{n(n-1)}$", "From our relation: $n(n-1)A - n(n+1)B = 2n+1$\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} = \\frac{2n+1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}$", "Wait: $n(n-1)A - n(n+1)B = 2n+1$\nDivide both sides by $n(n-1)(n+1)$:\n$\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} = \\frac{2n+1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}$", "Yes! That's what I need. Let me verify:\n$\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} = \\frac{2n+1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}$", "Then:\n$\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} + \\frac{1}{n(n^2-1)} = \\frac{2n+1}{n(n-1)(n+1)} + \\frac{1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}$", "$= \\frac{2n+2}{n(n-1)(n+1)} = \\frac{2(n+1)}{n(n-1)(n+1)} = \\frac{2}{n(n-1)}$", "So:\n$I = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\cdot\\frac{2}{n(n-1)} = 1$ ✓", "Great, so the integral equals 1.\n\nLet me write this up more carefully.", "Actually, let me redo the derivation from the start to make sure I have everything right.", "Starting integral:\n$$I = 4n(n-1)\\int_0^1 \\frac{1}{8t^3}\\left[\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n+1}}{n+1}-\\frac{t^{2n+2}}{n+1}-t^4\\left\\{\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n-1}}{n-1}-\\frac{t^{2n-2}}{n-1} \\right\\}\\right] dt$$", "Factor out $\\frac{4n(n-1)}{8} = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}$:", "$$I = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\int_0^1 \\frac{1}{t^3}\\left[\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n+1} - t^{2n+2}}{n+1} - \\frac{t^4\\left[(2t-t^2)^{n-1} - t^{2n-2}\\right]}{n-1}\\right] dt$$", "Using $(2t-t^2)^k = t^k(2-t)^k$:", "First term: $\\frac{t^{n+1}(2-t)^{n+1} - t^{2n+2}}{(n+1)t^3} = \\frac{t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1} - t^{2n-1}}{n+1}$", "Second term: $\\frac{t^4\\left[t^{n-1}(2-t)^{n-1} - t^{2n-2}\\right]}{(n-1)t^3} = \\frac{t\\cdot t^{n-1}(2-t)^{n-1} - t\\cdot t^{2n-2}}{n-1} = \\frac{t^n(2-t)^{n-1} - t^{2n-1}}{n-1}$", "So:\n$$I = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\int_0^1 \\left[\\frac{t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1} - t^{2n-1}}{n+1} - \\frac{t^n(2-t)^{n-1} - t^{2n-1}}{n-1}\\right] dt$$", "Split:\n$$I = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\left[\\frac{1}{n+1}\\int_0^1 t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1}dt - \\frac{1}{n+1}\\int_0^1 t^{2n-1}dt - \\frac{1}{n-1}\\int_0^1 t^n(2-t)^{n-1}dt + \\frac{1}{n-1}\\int_0^1 t^{2n-1}dt\\right]$$", "$= \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\left[\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} + \\frac{1}{2n}\\left(\\frac{1}{n-1} - \\frac{1}{n+1}\\right)\\right]$", "where $A = \\int_0^1 t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1}dt$, $B = \\int_0^1 t^n(2-t)^{n-1}dt$.", "$\\frac{1}{2n}\\left(\\frac{1}{n-1}-\\frac{1}{n+1}\\right) = \\frac{1}{2n}\\cdot\\frac{2}{n^2-1} = \\frac{1}{n(n^2-1)} = \\frac{1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}$", "So:\n$$I = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\left[\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} + \\frac{1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}\\right]$$", "Now, using integration by parts, we showed:\n- $C = \\int_0^1 t^{n-1}(2-t)^n dt$\n- $A = \\frac{1}{n-1} + \\frac{n+1}{n-1}C$\n- $B = C - \\frac{1}{n}$", "From $B = C - \\frac{1}{n}$: $C = B + \\frac{1}{n}$", "Substituting into $A$:\n$A = \\frac{1}{n-1} + \\frac{n+1}{n-1}\\left(B + \\frac{1}{n}\\right) = \\frac{1}{n-1} + \\frac{(n+1)B}{n-1} + \\frac{n+1}{n(n-1)}$", "$= \\frac{n + (n+1)B \\cdot n + n+1}{n(n-1)}$", "Wait, let me be more careful:\n$A = \\frac{1}{n-1} + \\frac{(n+1)B}{n-1} + \\frac{n+1}{n(n-1)}$", "To combine the first and third terms:\n$\\frac{1}{n-1} + \\frac{n+1}{n(n-1)} = \\frac{n + n+1}{n(n-1)} = \\frac{2n+1}{n(n-1)}$", "So: $A = \\frac{2n+1}{n(n-1)} + \\frac{(n+1)B}{n-1}$", "Multiply by $n(n-1)$:\n$n(n-1)A = 2n+1 + n(n+1)B$", "Therefore:\n$n(n-1)A - n(n+1)B = 2n+1$", "Dividing by $n(n-1)(n+1)$:\n$\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} = \\frac{2n+1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}$", "Substituting back:\n$I = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\left[\\frac{2n+1}{n(n-1)(n+1)} + \\frac{1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}\\right]$", "$= \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\cdot\\frac{2n+2}{n(n-1)(n+1)}$", "$= \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\cdot\\frac{2}{n(n-1)}$", "$= 1$ ✓\n\nThe integral equals 1 for $n \\geq 3$.\n\nNow let me write a clean solution."], "answer_text": "Looking at this problem, I need to evaluate:\n\n$$I = 4n(n-1)\\int_0^1 \\frac{1}{8t^3}\\left[\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n+1}-t^{2n+2}}{n+1}-t^4\\left\\{\\frac{(2t-t^2)^{n-1}-t^{2n-2}}{n-1}\\right\\}\\right] dt$$\n\n## Step 1: Simplify the Integrand\n\nFactoring out $\\frac{4n(n-1)}{8} = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}$ and using $(2t-t^2)^k = t^k(2-t)^k$:\n\n**First bracket** divided by $t^3$:\n$$\\frac{t^{n+1}(2-t)^{n+1}-t^{2n+2}}{(n+1)t^3} = \\frac{t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1}-t^{2n-1}}{n+1}$$\n\n**Second bracket** divided by $t^3$:\n$$\\frac{t^4[t^{n-1}(2-t)^{n-1}-t^{2n-2}]}{(n-1)t^3} = \\frac{t^n(2-t)^{n-1}-t^{2n-1}}{n-1}$$\n\nSo:\n$$I = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\left[\\frac{A}{n+1}-\\frac{B}{n-1}+\\frac{1}{2n}\\!\\left(\\frac{1}{n-1}-\\frac{1}{n+1}\\right)\\right]$$\n\nwhere $A=\\int_0^1 t^{n-2}(2-t)^{n+1}\\,dt$ and $B=\\int_0^1 t^n(2-t)^{n-1}\\,dt$.\n\nThe power term simplifies: $\\frac{1}{2n}\\cdot\\frac{2}{n^2-1} = \\frac{1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}$.\n\n## Step 2: Relate $A$ and $B$ via Integration by Parts\n\nDefine $C = \\int_0^1 t^{n-1}(2-t)^n\\,dt$.\n\n**For $A$:** Let $u=(2-t)^{n+1}$, $dv=t^{n-2}dt$, so $du=-(n+1)(2-t)^n dt$, $v=\\frac{t^{n-1}}{n-1}$:\n\n$$A = \\underbrace{\\left[\\frac{t^{n-1}(2-t)^{n+1}}{n-1}\\right]_0^1}_{=\\;\\frac{1}{n-1}} + \\frac{n+1}{n-1}C$$\n\n**For $B$:** Let $u=t^n$, $dv=(2-t)^{n-1}dt$, so $du=nt^{n-1}dt$, $v=-\\frac{(2-t)^n}{n}$:\n\n$$B = \\underbrace{\\left[-\\frac{t^n(2-t)^n}{n}\\right]_0^1}_{=\\;-\\frac{1}{n}} + C$$\n\nTherefore $C = B + \\frac{1}{n}$, and substituting into the expression for $A$:\n\n$$A = \\frac{1}{n-1} + \\frac{n+1}{n-1}\\!\\left(B+\\frac{1}{n}\\right) = \\frac{2n+1}{n(n-1)} + \\frac{(n+1)B}{n-1}$$\n\nMultiplying through by $n(n-1)$:\n\n$$\\boxed{n(n-1)A - n(n+1)B = 2n+1}$$\n\nDividing by $n(n-1)(n+1)$:\n\n$$\\frac{A}{n+1} - \\frac{B}{n-1} = \\frac{2n+1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}$$\n\n## Step 3: Substitute Back and Evaluate\n\n$$I = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\left[\\frac{2n+1}{n(n-1)(n+1)} + \\frac{1}{n(n-1)(n+1)}\\right] = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\cdot\\frac{2n+2}{n(n-1)(n+1)}$$\n\n$$I = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2}\\cdot\\frac{2}{n(n-1)} = 1$$\n\n## Verification for $n=3$\n\n- $A = \\int_0^1 t(2-t)^4\\,dt = \\frac{3}{2}$, $\\quad B = \\int_0^1 t^3(2-t)^2\\,dt = \\frac{1}{6}$\n- $n(n-1)A - n(n+1)B = 6\\cdot\\frac{3}{2} - 12\\cdot\\frac{1}{6} = 9 - 2 = 7 = 2(3)+1$ ✓\n\n$$\\boxed{1}$$", "annotations": {"27B·v4": {"nodes": [{"node_id": 0, "p_start": 0, "p_end": 1, "label": "SU", "deps": [], "branch": 0, "path": "M", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 1, "p_start": 2, "p_end": 4, "label": "CP", "deps": [0], "branch": 0, "path": "M", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 2, "p_start": 5, "p_end": 7, "label": "CP", "deps": [1], "branch": 0, "path": "M", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 3, "p_start": 8, "p_end": 11, "label": "CP", "deps": [2], "branch": 0, "path": "M", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 4, "p_start": 12, "p_end": 12, "label": "EX", "deps": [3], "branch": 1, "path": "A", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 5, "p_start": 13, "p_end": 16, "label": "CP", "deps": [4], "branch": 1, "path": "A", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 6, "p_start": 17, "p_end": 17, "label": "MB", "deps": [5], "branch": 1, "path": "A", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 7, "p_start": 18, "p_end": 18, "label": "EX", "deps": [3], "branch": 2, "path": "A", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 8, "p_start": 19, "p_end": 21, "label": "CP", "deps": [7], "branch": 2, "path": "A", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 9, "p_start": 22, "p_end": 22, "label": "MB", "deps": [8], "branch": 2, "path": "A", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 10, "p_start": 23, "p_end": 23, "label": "EX", "deps": [3], "branch": 3, "path": "A", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 11, "p_start": 24, "p_end": 25, "label": "CP", "deps": [10], "branch": 3, "path": "A", "flags": ""}, {"node_id": 12, "p_start": 26, "p_end": 26, "label": "MB", "deps": [11], "branch": 3, "path": "A", "flags": ""}, {"node_i